(c)YA3 is the data from the meter labelled “Machine Paid External Bonus Payout” for the reporting period;
(d)YA4 is the data from the meter labelled “Machine Paid Progressive Payout” for the reporting period;
(e)YA5 is the data from the meter labelled “Attendant Paid Jackpots” for the reporting period;
(f)YA6 is the data from the meter labelled “Attendant Paid External Bonus Payout” for the reporting period; and
(g)YA7 is the data from the meter labelled “Attendant Paid Progressive Payout” for the reporting period.
(2) There must be allowed to a casino operator a deduction from the net win computed in accordance with paragraph (1) of any other prize not recorded by the meters of the gaming program referred to in that paragraph, which was paid out by the casino operator to any player as winnings on a game played on the gaming program, as a result of the player having placed a bet on the game.
(3) Where, in the opinion of the Comptroller, the net win for any gaming program or programs in a reporting period or any part thereof cannot be determined with reasonable accuracy under paragraph (1), due to —
(a)a malfunction of the gaming program or programs or the electronic device or devices used with the gaming program or programs to play the game or games;
(b)an adjustment of any meter of a gaming program for which no reasonable explanation has been given to the satisfaction of the Comptroller; or
(c)for any other reason,
